Milo was a small gray cat who lived in a quiet house at the end of Maple Street. He spent most of his days napping in sunbeams, chasing dust motes, and watching birds from the windowsill. But one morning, a strange sound came from the garden.

It was a soft, tinkling sound, like tiny bells.

Milo’s ears twitched. He padded outside and found a small silver key half-buried in the grass. It was warm to the touch and glimmered even though the sky was cloudy.

As soon as he touched it with his paw, the garden gate creaked open by itself.

Milo had never left the garden before. He hesitated, then stepped forward.

