At the end of the path stood a crooked old house with a door made of blue glass. A black cat sat on the steps, wearing a tiny brass collar.

“You found the key,” the black cat said.

Milo blinked. “You can talk?”

“Only when it matters,” the cat replied. “I’m Bramble. And you’ve been chosen.”

“Chosen for what?”

